{
  "id": "controller-prototype",
  "content": {
    "description": [
      [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "In Interaction Experience/Design (third year), we re-examined daily interactions with an everyday device and designed a tangible interface to enhance or replace part of that interaction. I focused on projectors: presenters often point at slides, but those gestures are not responsive; highlighting text, manipulating 3D models, or triggering embedded media still requires reaching the host computer or a helper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "The controller, initially conceived as a glove, was meant to let presenters interact gesturally with projected content, supporting clearer, more engaging classroom presentations."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    ],
